# Diagnostics
```
invalid-astro-template-writes.astro:2:1 lint/style/useConst  FIXABLE  ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

  ! This let declares a variable that is only assigned once.
  
    1 │ ---
  > 2 │ let constant = "constant";
      │ ^^^
    3 │ let written = "before";
    4 │ let mutated = 0;
  
  i 'constant' is never reassigned.
  
    1 │ ---
  > 2 │ let constant = "constant";
      │     ^^^^^^^^
    3 │ let written = "before";
    4 │ let mutated = 0;
  
  i A variable that is never reassigned is clearer as const, because it prevents the binding from being reassigned.
  
  i Safe fix: Use const instead.
  
    1   │ - let·constant·=·"constant";
      1 │ + const·constant·=·"constant";
    2 2 │   let written = "before";
    3 3 │   let mutated = 0;
  

```

